Sval: give the tab an agent works in the focus of a focused window

Pages depend on focus: form libraries validate a field on blur, comboboxes
open on focus, and pages check document.hasFocus(). Gecko gives that only to
the tab in the active window (nsFocusManager::SetFocusInner sends focus and
blur and sets :focus only for an element there, and Document::HasFocus asks
IsInActiveWindow), and it keeps one focused window per process, mirrored to
the parent. Moving that focus into an agent's tab takes the user's keyboard,
so no chrome API can give the agent's page focus. This adds a parent-set
BrowsingContext field, SvalFocusEmulated, and hooks in HasFocus,
SetFocusInner's inactive-window branch, ClearFocus and WindowLowered that
hand over to Sval's SvalFocusEmulation.cpp. There the tab's pages hear focus
and blur and match :focus, :focus-visible and :focus-within as in a focused
window, with the focus manager's own NotifyFocusStateChange and
SendFocusOrBlurEvent, while the process's focused window, the parent and the
widgets are left alone. The emulated events are kept from the accessibility
service, so what a screen reader follows is the real focus. Real focus wins:
nothing is emulated while the tab is in the active window, and a tab lowered
from it gets its emulated focus back.

